# The account that pays for moving a phase on when its deadline passes.
#
# It needs funding and nothing else. `advance_phase` asks for no signature, so
# this address holds no authority the public does not hold: anybody could send
# the same call and the contract could not tell the two apart. Its own key
# rather than the sealer's, because the sealer's address is named in the
# constitution and should not also be running errands.
#
# Without it the clock will not start, and phases wait for somebody to press the
# button on the manage page.
CLOCK_SECRET_KEY=""

# How long between laps, in milliseconds. This is the worst case a deadline can
# be late by. Default 30000.
CLOCK_EVERY_MS=""

# Which hackathon the indexer follows when the whole backend is started with
# `npm run dev`. It takes one contract at a time, so this is how somebody
# switches between events without editing a command.
#
# Only `npm run dev` reads it. Running the indexer directly still takes the
# address as an argument.
# Narrows the indexer to one hackathon. Left empty it follows every hackathon
# in the database, which is what you want unless you are debugging one event.
WATCH_CONTRACT=""
